<i>Posted by Kaludram on 11-21-2002 07:35 PM:</i>

<p><b> </b></p>

<p>In my experience nothing holds true.   Dueling on a blue server is a wholly different world from true pvp on red servers where you never know what gear the guy has or how competent they are.  The best caster PKer will easily be beaten by gear if his opponent is melee with a close eye on his resists.  I have seen it time and time again, especially with the somewhat modified resist rules on pvp servers.  <br />
<br />
I would say your guide will be most useful on blue servers when you choose the time and place for combat.  I would also suggest, since your example contains no mention of it, an extensive list of easily aquired click items that can turn loss to victory in a real pvp environment.  I know on Rallos I typically have a single bag, all other inv slots are filled with clickable, hotkeyed items ready for the fool that wants to die.<br />
<br />
Unfortunately, the real masters of PKing generally do not say a single word about their PK skill anywhere.   They just do what they have to do, and have no need to brag about it because their name is whispered by those in the know.  They are not the fellows you see on the red server message boards lying about never having been PKed, because everyone has.  You do not become the best without failing and finding out your weaknesses.<br />
<br />
However, I do look forward to reading your guide.  It should contain some accurate information for pvp in cases of equivalent competency.<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" class="nf">__________________<br>
Kaludram Aderlas, Master of Shadows for the <a href="http://pub59.ezboard.com/bshadowcongress4908" target="_blank"><i> Shadow Congress </i></a><br />
</font></p></p>
